WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
SCP-682 Vs SCP-858.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.400
Could Gravity’s Rainbow finally clear the
dark cloud of the unkillable reptile, and

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.120
bring sunny skies to the SCP Foundation?

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.520
A tissue sample from 682, repelled from Earth’s
gravity at a speed of 9.8 m/s was destroyed

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.360
by SCP-858.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.120
When SCP-682 was exposed to 858, it began
to fall away from the Earth’s surface at

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.880
the same rate as the sample.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.000
It reached 858, but it did not disappear.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.720
It hit some sort of invisible barrier, and
its body appeared to be slowly boiling.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.400
This continued until the reptile had lost
50% of its body mass.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.440
When half of its body was gone, 682 suddenly
sprouted a pair of wings similar to those

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.080
of pterosaurs, in addition to an array of
air bladders that allowed it to fly perpendicular

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.400
to SCP-858’s gravity.

